Explain why a newly uploaded object may not transition immediately and mention relevant storage-duration or object-size considerations. 

A newly uploaded object may not transition immediately because:
- The rule specifies a 30-day waiting period.
- S3 lifecycle processing is asynchronous.
- The object must meet the applicable transition requirements.
- Objects smaller than the minimum eligible size may not transition under the default size constraints.

Example: An object uploaded to backups/ today becomes eligible for the configured transition after 30 days, assuming it meets all requirements.
